! store_into_prepared_instr.strap -- an instruction whose word a pending
! look-ahead level is going to store into is not prepared until that
! store has been made.
!
! FOUND 2026-11-17 by the 7030 STRAP II TABMAN test (tests/
! check_strap2_7030_tabman.py, step 3b, call 24 ADDORD 3 11), when the
! preparation floor was fixed (StretchCore's `ib` and the level load's
! "- 1") and the I-box ran further ahead.  TBEN2's tail sets the length of
! its own store, "ST(BU,6),TBEN4+.35", then "LV,$4,TBQ", "L(BU,24),TBK",
! and TBEN4 "ST(BU,64),0($4)" stores the vle's address with the length
! just written.  TBEN4 was prepared into a level from 1Y/2Y while the
! ST(BU,6) level was still pending behind a slow E-box, so it ran with
! the length the deck was assembled with (64), and the entry's function
! field lost the address: table 3's second word came back
! (16)40000002C0000000 for (16)40000002C49D9800.
!
! THE MODEL HAD HALF OF IT.  The program store compare (StretchIBox's
! mkInstrBuffers, Blosk p.21) invalidates a Y word when a store to it is
! MADE.  An instruction already prepared out of that word is past the Y
! buffers by then.  Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-21 (PDF 39, read in the
! page image), "Store Close to Fetch": "One such conflict is a store into a
! location corresponding to a prefetched instruction ... The second
! instruction, having been previously fetched into 1Y or 2Y, clearly
! cannot have the correct information until the store is complete. When
! such a store is decoded, I-box invalidates the prefetched instructions
! and waits until the correct information is available."  The fix
! (rl_prepare, `instrStored`) does not prepare an instruction whose word
! (either word, for a full-word instruction) a pending level stores.
! CHOSEN: the 7030 waits at the decoding of the STORE when its address is
! a prefetched word; the model waits at the preparation of the instruction
! in that word, which holds the same instructions back and lets the ones
! between the store and the stored word run.
!
! CASE 1, the hazard: LTRS(BU,64,8), 60 clocks in the E-box (PDF 123),
! keeps the levels behind it pending.  LI 24 and ST(BU,6) into MOD's
! length field; LVI $4 = W0; LI (8)12345670; MOD "ST(BU,64),0($4)", which
! runs as ST(BU,24).  W0 starts all ones.
!   W0 = (16)29CBB8FFFFFFFFFF   (stale: (16)000000000029CBB8)
! CASE 2, the control: the same into MOD2 and W1 with an unconditional
! branch between the length store and MOD2.  The branch drains the
! look-ahead (StretchIBox's iboxHazard), so the store is made before MOD2
! is prepared, with or without the fix.
!   W1 = (16)29CBB8FFFFFFFFFF
! Values hand-derived from the field positions (RefMan printed pp.21, 58).
!
! INJECTIONS, measured 2026-11-17, restored from a saved copy checked with
! cmp:
!   - the gate removed (`else if (False && instrStored)`): FAIL W0 =
!     (16)29CBB8, cycles 252 against 244; W1 (the control) passes.
!   - the gate without its recentStore() term (the first version):
!     the same FAIL W0, cycles 252.
!   - the preparation floor removed: W0 and W1 pass, cycles 246.
! The base model (2cee08a) fails case 1 the same way (W0 = (16)29CBB8,
! 254 clocks): the hazard predates the floor fix.
! CYCLES 244 is the model as of this change.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   LTRS(BU,64,8), SLOW
        LI(BU,6), 24
        ST(BU,6), MOD+.35
        LVI, $4, W0
        LI(BU,24), (8)12345670
MOD     ST(BU,64), 0($4)
        LI(BU,6), 24
        ST(BU,6), MOD2+.35
        LVI, $4, W1
        LI(BU,24), (8)12345670
        B, MOD2
MOD2    ST(BU,64), 0($4)
DONE    BEW, $
        SLC, 1100.0
SLOW    DD(BU,64), 0
W0      DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
W1      DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
        END, START
